--   Counted loop with an item-language body (round six, `irep`)
-- statement:
--   **Counted loop with an item-language body** (managed states, as `Sp.rep`).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KIL6Loop`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KIL.IRuns.irep {C : Fin HS} {n : Ex HS} {body : IStmt HS Pp} {s : IState HS}
--       {F : ℕ → Fin HS → List ℤ} {N B c : ℕ} (hB1 : 1 ≤ B) (hC5 : C.val < 56) (hC : ∀ k, F k C = [])
--       (hnc : n.Clean) (hno : n.ok (encK s (F 0))) (hnl : n.Lin) (hnb : n.Bnd (encK s (F 0)) B)
--       (hn : n.eval (encK s (F 0)) = N)
--       (hb : ∀ k < N, IRuns I iprog body (encK s (Function.update (F k) C [(N : ℤ) - k]))
--         (encK s (Function.update (F (k + 1)) C [(N : ℤ) - k])) c) :
--       IRuns I iprog (NLogN.KIL.irep C n body) (encK s (F 0)) (encK s (F N))
--         ((n.size + 1) * 2000 * (B + 2) + N * (c + 8000 * (B + 2) + 30) + (2 * B + 32))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** KIL6: counted loops whose body is item-language code (with procedure calls)
--
--   `irep C n body` is the item-language counterpart of `RS.rep C n b` for an arbitrary
--   `IStmt` body (which may contain `.call`s): push the count `n` on the counter stack `C`, run
--   `body; C := C - 1` while the top of `C` is nonzero, pop `C`.  `IRuns.irep` is the analogue of
--   `Sp.rep` on managed states.
--
--   Also: `Sp.asgQ` (assignment of a general expression, quadratic cost) and the conversion of a
--   stack-`0` specification on `t.upd 0 …` states to managed states (`Sp.top0`).
